course: dictionary
lesson: 12487
title: Demographic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A demographic is a group of people who share something, such as their age or where they live. The word is long, but its parts give a clue: demo means people, and graphic means written or drawn, so it is about recording facts about people.
explain: «The bike company wants to reach the teenage demographic.» The clues are company, reach and teenage. A company wants to sell to a group of people, so a demographic is a group of people it hopes will buy from it.
explain: «The town's demographics show that more people are now over 65.» Demographics is the plural form. The clues are town and over 65, so demographics means facts and numbers about a population: how many people there are, how old they are, and where they live.
explain: Demographic can also be an adjective, as in «demographic data». It means to do with the study of populations. Swap in your meaning: «data about the study of populations» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: A demographic is a group of people with something in common, such as age or where they live.
fact: Demographics are facts and numbers about a population: how many people there are, how old they are and where they live.
fact: As an adjective, demographic means to do with the study of populations, as in «demographic data».
fact: «The target demographic» is the group of people a company hopes will buy its product.
fact: Demographic data often appears in geography and maths as graphs and population pyramids.
exercise: «The bike company wants to reach the teenage demographic.» What is a demographic here? | A type of bicycle | *A group of people with something in common | A kind of map | A shop that sells food
exercise: «The town's demographics show that more people are now over 65.» What are demographics? | *Facts and numbers about the people who live in a town | The names of the streets | Rules for driving cars | Tall buildings in the town centre
exercise: In «demographic data», what does demographic describe? | *Something to do with the study of populations | Something that is very loud | Something made of wood | Something that happens only at night
test: «The target demographic for the new game is children aged nine to twelve.» What does target demographic mean? | The place where the game is sold | *A group of people a company hopes will buy its product | A game that is too hard | A list of rules for the game
test: Which word means facts and numbers about how many people live somewhere and how old they are? | Geography | *Demographics | Graphics | Democracy
exam: «Demographic change» in a town might mean what? | The buildings are painted a new colour | *The number and ages of the people living there shift over time | The roads are closed for repairs | The trees lose their leaves in autumn
